WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.040
Every cup of coffee begins as fruit.

2
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:20.780
A cherry, ripening slowly on a
mountain, where the nights are cool.

3
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:23.210
Cool nights slow it down.

4
00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:25.780
And slow means sweet.

5
00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:30.010
When it turns deep red,
it's picked by hand.

6
00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:32.860
Often, one cherry at a time.

7
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.180
Now, look inside.

8
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:40.020
Under the skin, a sweet fruit pulp.

9
00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:43.940
Then a sticky, sugary layer: the mucilage.

10
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.280
A papery shell, called parchment.

11
00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.950
And at the heart, two seeds.

12
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.680
Those seeds are your coffee beans.

13
00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:57.277
Before a bean can travel, it has to dry.

14
00:00:57.327 --> 00:01:02.740
And how much fruit stays on it while it
dries changes everything you'll taste.

15
00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:07.290
Washed. The fruit is stripped away.

16
00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:12.330
The sticky layer ferments loose, is rinsed
off, and the clean seed dries in its

17
00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:13.740
shell.

18
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:20.000
Bright. Crisp. Clear. You taste
the bean, and the place it grew.

19
00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:27.530
Natural. The whole cherry dries in the
sun, for weeks, turned by hand, day after

20
00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:28.780
day.

21
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.590
The seed soaks up the fruit around it.

22
00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:36.600
Jammy, wild and winey. Think
blueberry, and strawberry.

23
00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:44.180
Honey. No bees involved. The skin comes
off, but the sticky layer stays on.

24
00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:46.930
Leave a little: yellow honey.

25
00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:51.340
More: red. Almost all of it: black.

26
00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:55.260
Sweet and round, right
between washed and natural.

27
00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:02.780
Anaerobic. Sealed in a tank, without
oxygen, the fruit ferments slowly, and on

28
00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:06.380
purpose. Bold, boozy, tropical.

29
00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:10.370
Wet-hulled, the Sumatran way.

30
00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:13.650
The shell comes off while
the seed is still wet.

31
00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:17.340
Earthy, cedar, heavy and deep.

32
00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:21.730
And at the frontier: carbonic maceration.

33
00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:24.210
Co-ferments. Thermal shock.

34
00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:26.660
Producers keep inventing.

35
00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:30.550
Once it's dry, the shell is milled away.

36
00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:34.040
Every bean is sorted, and packed in jute.

37
00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:39.500
Then, still green, it crosses
an ocean, to a roaster.

38
00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:43.810
Heat turns it gold, then brown.

39
00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:47.940
Its sugars caramelise, and
it cracks, like popcorn.

40
00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:53.520
It rests for a week or two,
while it lets go of its gas.

41
00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:57.600
And then, finally, it's yours.

42
00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:03.930
So much of what's in this cup, the berry,
the sweetness, the brightness, was decided

43
00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:07.500
months ago, by a farmer's
choice about fruit.

44
00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:14.240
Crema looks up your coffee, shows
you its journey, and how to brew it.

45
00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:16.620
Taste where it's been.

